<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador coffee exports fell 19 pct in Jan-Oct.</title>
<headline>Ecuador coffee exports fell 19 pct in Jan-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's coffee exports fell 19 percent in the first 10 months of 1996 to 1.28 million 60-kg bags due to the retention plan of the Association of Coffee Producing Countries (ACPC), an exporters group said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The National Coffee Exporter's Association said Ecuador shipped 1.58 million bags in the first 10 months of 1995.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, coffee revenues fell 33.8 percent in the January-October period to $135.3 million from $204.5 million in the comparable period of 1995.</p>
<p>Ecuador plans to export 1.4 million bags between July of this year and June 1997.</p>
<p>Coffee is Ecuador's fifth export earner, after oil, banana, shrimp and cacao.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
